725
00:53:29.930 --> 00:53:33.470
In PowerPoint polish EBC decks
and exec decks [phonetic]

726
00:53:33.470 --> 00:53:38.740
often have complex visuals
with a lot of little pieces
like the lines, dots, etc.

727
00:53:39.370 --> 00:53:42.530
What is the guidance for alt
text, decorative, etc.?

728
00:53:42.870 --> 00:53:48.020
Is there a way to group
everything together within a
slide in a hidden way that can

729
00:53:48.020 --> 00:53:53.570
be grouped together with a
single description or other
best practices in these cases?

730
00:53:54.380 --> 00:53:57.730
&gt;&gt; Sure, that's a really
good question and something
we do actually see a lot.

731
00:53:58.790 --> 00:54:00.310
There's lots of scenarios
where someone might

732
00:54:00.310 --> 00:54:03.220
have really complicated visuals
that have lots of objects.

733
00:54:04.690 --> 00:54:09.160
Whenever possible, we
recommend simplifying
that as much as you can.

734
00:54:09.810 --> 00:54:12.660
If you don't need quite so
many of the objects, you

735
00:54:12.660 --> 00:54:16.720
can hide them, mark
them as decorative, but
you can group things.

736
00:54:16.720 --> 00:54:18.156
That helps a lot.

737
00:54:18.770 --> 00:54:21.880
So these slides I have
today aren't very complex

738
00:54:21.880 --> 00:54:24.460
so I don't have a
great example here, but

739
00:54:24.460 --> 00:54:27.750
if I had a really complex slide,
I could group the objects together

740
00:54:28.230 --> 00:54:30.530
and then in the reading
order pane, they would
show in that group.

741
00:54:32.500 --> 00:54:36.290
If it's a really complex visual
that just has lots of pieces but

742
00:54:36.290 --> 00:54:42.550
it's indicating one thing,
one approach that I've seen
a lot is if you select each

743
00:54:42.550 --> 00:54:47.620
of those objects that are
conveying one thing, copy
cutting them from the slide

744
00:54:47.620 --> 00:54:52.630
and then pasting them as
an image and then giving
that image alt text -

745
00:54:53.130 --> 00:54:57.680
because if the goal is for
your visual to have just kind
of one key take away from it,

746
00:54:58.640 --> 00:55:01.580
as much as you can do
that, kind

747
00:55:01.580 --> 00:55:06.180
of distill it down into one
image and give alt text to that.

748
00:55:06.880 --> 00:55:10.640
I don't have a great example.

749
00:55:10.640 --> 00:55:16.590
Let me see if I can mock
one up just really quick.

750
00:55:16.590 --> 00:55:18.724
I'll just add a
couple symbols.

751
00:55:29.060 --> 00:55:31.730
&gt;&gt; I think there was
a follow-up to that.

752
00:55:31.730 --> 00:55:32.920
So let me keep reading.

753
00:55:32.920 --> 00:55:37.960
The desired outcome is
that each line and dot
would be considered in and

754
00:55:37.960 --> 00:55:39.710
of itself decorative,
but the sum

755
00:55:39.710 --> 00:55:42.730
of all the little components
would be a single visual ID.

756
00:55:44.190 --> 00:55:46.610
What is [indiscernible]
to give a description for?

757
00:55:47.480 --> 00:55:48.890
Anyway to achieve
this outcome?

758
00:55:48.890 --> 00:55:52.000
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so in what
I'm creating right now.

759
00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:55.500
Let's say that I've just
added a simple chart,

760
00:55:55.500 --> 00:55:58.680
but maybe these triangles
are indicating some sort

761
00:55:58.680 --> 00:56:02.490
of up and down diagram,
trend or something like that.

762
00:56:03.200 --> 00:56:05.180
But each of them is
a discrete object.

763
00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:10.220
So what I can do is I'll cut them
from the slide and then paste them

764
00:56:10.220 --> 00:56:13.100
as image and so
now they're still

765
00:56:13.100 --> 00:56:16.630
the same visual but it's just
one object to give alt text.

766
00:56:16.630 --> 00:56:18.370
&gt;&gt; Yeah,
but the only challenge is that -

767
00:56:18.370 --> 00:56:21.480
and, again, this coming from David
- the only challenge is that if

768
00:56:21.790 --> 00:56:26.770
we paste it as image, you
lose ability to animate
the complex diagram.

769
00:56:26.770 --> 00:56:31.280
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I think to be
transparent, there's not

770
00:56:31.280 --> 00:56:34.190
a perfect answer that I can
give today, unfortunately.

771
00:56:36.440 --> 00:56:41.550
Whenever possible, make those
things as flat as you can, and so

772
00:56:41.550 --> 00:56:46.270
if there are things that
animate in together, maybe
those could be a group.

773
00:56:47.540 --> 00:56:51.020
But just wherever possible,
think about how you can reduce

774
00:56:51.020 --> 00:56:55.800
the number of discrete
objects, either by grouping
or pasting as image.

775
00:56:55.801 --> 00:56:58.722
I know that's not a great
answer, but --

